WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.580
Hey what's up guys it's Rob and welcome
to my tutorial for:

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.140
The Transforming Ninja Star!

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:07.240
 

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.650
Similar to the eight-pointed ninja star this is an all new four pointed one that I designed

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:14.380
together with Jeremy Shafer. You can check out his tutorial by clicking on this link up here

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.840
It also changes from a frisbee into
a ninja star with two simple moves

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.529
Making it requires four square sheets of
any size I'm going to be using two

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:25.830
different color printer sheets that I
will split into quarters but if you want

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.830
to use one sheet or you can even try to
make a super one by using the whole

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.859
printer sheet it's totally up to you. So
once you have the paper ,let's get

00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:35.190
started. If you'd like to have two
different colors in your star like mine,

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:39.420
we'll need to split two different sheets.
Once we have the four squares we can

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.040
turn each into these modular units which
are all identical. Once we finish making

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.789
four we can then interlock them to
finish the star. Take both sheets and

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:51.930
fold them in half lengthwise making a
nice sharp crease down the edge. We can

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:55.289
then split them by tearing them or
cutting them. Set the other two pieces

00:00:55.289 --> 00:00:59.820
aside. Fold both shorter outer sides onto
the longer side and once again cut or

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:03.570
tear along the edges. This makes four
squares measuring 4.25 inches if you're

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.470
using letter size paper. Now that we have the four squares we can

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:11.250
go on to make the modular units. Remember, they're all made the exact same way so

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:14.400
I'll go through with you how to make one
of them and then you can make the others

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.320
on your own. Grab one of the sheets and
let's get started since we now have a

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.680
crease in the paper going diagonally
this way we're gonna make one going this

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.520
way by taking the upper left corner and
folding it down to the bottom right

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.600
corner. Once the corners are lined up,
just make a nice sharp crease on the

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.540
upper left here all throughout the paper
with your fingernail

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.950
because sharp creases will make it a lot
easier to make the modules. You can open

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.430
up the paper again and you'll see we now
have an X in it. We're going to take the

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:46.079
top and fold it down to the bottom once
again lining up the edges as neatly as

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:51.030
you can and making a nice sharp crease
on the top now. When you open up the

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.689
paper, just hold the edges so that
they're facing downwards and all the

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:58.710
folds are Mountain folds-- as you'll see
we have a little upside-down V or

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:02.280
mountain in the paper. Then we can take
the two top corners and we're going to

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:06.420
airplane fold them directly into the
middle like this so that the top edge

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:11.280
lies on the midline and the corner is on
the center point. Line it up as neatly as

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:16.740
possible and then we can make a
crease on the outside. Do the same with

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:20.910
the upper left corner: just fold it
directly next to the other one trying to

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:26.160
be as neat as possible, and make another
sharp crease. Now we could take the

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.150
outside edge here and 
fold it directly onto this diagonal

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:35.820
crease. Fold it like this just round it
off so that the tip here lines up on

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:42.090
this point and the edge on the diagonal.
Now we're going to crease the edge here

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:47.490
from this horizontal crease all the way
down so just press right here and just

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:51.480
crease it like that making sure that
it's lined up then we can just run our

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:56.970
fingernail against the outside edge. Now
we can open it up and do the same with

00:02:56.970 --> 00:03:02.850
the left side: take the edge round it off,
line it up like that and we're going to

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:07.610
crease it from this horizontal crease
right here all the way down the paper

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:12.090
Once again, just run your fingernail
against it. Then you can open it up now

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:15.930
you'll see we folded these little
triangles and they've gotten folded back

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:19.980
We're just gonna pick up the corner here
and we're gonna tuck this triangle or

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:26.040
tip right on the inside by folding it
down and then flattening it back out. So

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:31.800
just tug the corner, fold downwards on
the triangle here and fold it back down.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.760
Then we could flatten it once again so
we should have something that looks like

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.239
this. I'm going to take these two edges
and we're going to push them together

00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:43.890
like this and we're just gonna pinch the
top point. We're going to take this edge

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:48.209
and we're going to push upwards on it
like this and if you made that crease so

00:03:48.209 --> 00:03:52.230
that it's a mountain fold it should kind
of get pointed upwards like that like a

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:56.430
little triangle. Just take it lift it up
and then we could take these two edges

00:03:56.430 --> 00:04:01.980
and flatten them together like this. Then,
we could just flatten the paper once

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:07.170
again. Now you'll see we have this
triangle that's on top and we're just

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:10.799
going to take the point of the triangle
and fold it right onto this

00:04:10.799 --> 00:04:15.390
little corner here just rounding it off
and meeting it up with that point on

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:20.489
this crease here. Once it's lined up like
that then we could just make a nice

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:25.770
sharp crease on the top. Now we can
unfold it and we're just going to open

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:29.820
up these two edges here
holding it like this and just spreading

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:33.840
it open like that. You'll see we have
this big triangle and the little

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.250
triangle: We're gonna press on the big
triangle so that this big triangle

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:42.900
that's all the way on top is going
downward. So we're gonna invert it or

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:48.600
reverse fold it by pressing downwards on
this edge like this just like that and

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:53.660
just press downwards and then we could
squeeze the two edges together like this

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:57.780
Now you'll see we have this little
triangle on the bottom we're just gonna

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:03.150
flip it over and we're gonna do the same
thing. Open up the two edges hold it like

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:08.400
this and just press on this edge so that
the triangle gets inverted or reverse

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:17.160
folded by pressing downwards on the top.
Push down and flatten it out so you

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:20.760
should have a piece of paper that looks
just like this and you finished the

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:24.360
first module. We're just going to make
three more of these and then we could

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:28.180
join them together.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:38.420
Now that we've
completed the four modules, we can

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:43.080
interlock them together in order to
finish the transforming ninja star. Each

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:49.680
module has a point and also two tips or
flaps which will lock into the back of

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:55.710
the next piece and slide in a groove or
track just like that. We're going to hold

00:05:55.710 --> 00:06:00.450
two pieces so that the point is on the
left side and the flaps are on the right

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.300
side. Remember, the flaps are where we tucked in those

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:07.740
little triangles into the center on the
right side. You'll notice that right next

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.550
to the point here you should have a
little crease that I've marked here on

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:15.450
the paper. We're going to be using
that as a guide. We can turn the piece

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:20.310
on the right 90 degrees like this and
we're going to place it in between the two

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:25.140
flaps here all the way against the base
of that triangle until it doesn't go

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:26.820
anymore. Now to make sure that they're

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:31.290
perpendicular all we need to do is just
slide it up until the bottom of these

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:35.430
flaps here align with that little crease.
We could just hold it there like

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:41.340
this. We're going to fold this top flap
away and the back flap

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:45.750
towards us so that we can slide it in
between here. Just hold this flap back

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:51.360
and we can fold this one down like
this let go the back one and fold it

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:56.820
towards us. Give it a little pinch, and
then you could unfold it. Then all we

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:01.770
need to do is to just slide it right in
between the groove here just like this

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:08.040
and the back one will go next to it like
that. Then you can close it and give

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:15.290
it a little pinch. Then what we need to
do is just slide it back and forth and

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:20.100
break it in a little bit. Now that
we've done that we can move on to the

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:24.600
next one. In my case I have blue, red...
I'm going to take a blue one and do the

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:29.639
same thing. Slide the one on the right in
between the two flaps and align the

00:07:29.639 --> 00:07:34.260
bottom of it here with that little
crease. Then hold it, take the back one

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:40.080
fold it away and crease that little tip
over let go the back one and take the

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.229
back tip and fold it towards me just
give it a little pinch

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:48.870
unfold them and tuck them into that
little groove on this side and the back

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:54.360
one goes on the other side. Give it a
little pinch and once again just break

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:58.830
it in a little bit. Now all we need to do
is the last one. Take the last one and do

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:02.370
the same exact thing. If they start to
get a little bent it's okay, we're just

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:08.310
joining this one now. So just put it in
here, seat it all the way and place it on

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:14.760
that crease. Take the back flap hold it
back fold this over let go hold this one

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:20.010
towards you. Give it a little pinch
unfold them and then tuck them into that

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:26.099
groove. Give it a pinch and we can once
again break it in a little bit.

00:08:26.099 --> 00:08:30.960
Now you'll notice in the middle here there's a little piece that the flaps can

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:34.830
sometimes go over like that even though
it's supposed to kind of stay on the

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:38.909
side. That's okay as long as you just
kind of break it in and it finds its own

00:08:38.909 --> 00:08:43.589
little path. Now for the last one we're
just going to slide the first one in

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:48.330
between the two flaps of the last when we just joined just like that and once

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:51.630
again make sure that they're
perpendicular and do the same exact

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:58.270
thing. Hold the back one fold this over
and fold this one towards you. Then all

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:03.520
we need to do is just tuck it in like this
by opening it up and tucking it

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:11.110
in there. Same thing with this one tuck
it in there and give it a pinch. Then

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:14.680
all we need to do is just break it in a
little bit so if it pops out that's okay

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:19.510
Just slide it back and forth like
that take the two opposite ones and just

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:25.330
kind of push it back and forth do the
same thing this way and then to

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.810
transform it you just take the two
opposite points push them together like

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:34.270
this turn it clockwise 90 degrees take
the two ends and push it like that.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:39.550
Then to open it you just pull it let's
pull it here and pull it here and there

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:45.850
you go there's your Transforming Ninja
Star! In the untransformed state it flies

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:50.770
just like a frisbee so I put my finger
right here on the tip here and I flick

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:55.100
my wrist out holding it pretty much
horizontal.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:58.500
Let's try the super one!

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.950
Oh, right in my face!

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:13.420
In the transformed configuration you could do it the same way just put your finger

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:17.800
on the end here and flick it like a
frisbee. Or you can also throw it

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:20.520
vertically like this

